      "section": "star-constellation-heavens-wills-guidance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_purple_mountain_true_monarch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The founding is recorded as an inference with named premises, not as a dated event. Chapter 1737 is titled “Heavenly Court’s Foundation”.",
      "chapters": [
        1737
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1738 is titled “Primordial Origin Heavenly Court!”. In that stretch Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable announces that his sect will be named Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        1738
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_primordial_origin_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "That is strong evidence of the founding link. It is still not a calendar date for when the Court began.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1747 is titled “Star Constellation’s Sacrifice”. Under that title, Duke Long recounts that when Star Constellation Immortal Venerable’s lifespan was near its end, she sacrificed herself and assimilated with the Dao so her will could participate in the operations of the Heavenly Dao and keep fate Gu in Heavenly Court’s grasp.",
      "chapters": [
        1747
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_heavenly_dao"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Court is also under pressure by this point. Chapter 1707 is titled “Heavenly Court’s Crisis”.",
      "chapters": [
        1707
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1711 names a Heavenly Court battlefield.",
      "chapters": [
        1711
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1715 has the Court awakening.",
      "chapters": [
        1715
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A little later a chapter is given to its righteousness.",
      "chapters": [
        1818
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The title names righteousness; the chapter does not by itself prove that the Court is the sole righteous pole of the novel’s central divide.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-and-later-arrangements",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The last arc of the novel is named for the Court. Inside the Heavenly Court Final War arc, the Court’s own crushing defeat carries a chapter title.",
      "chapters": [
        2305
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
